.el .ds Aq '
.TH sway-things 1 "" "Sway Things 0.0.0" "Sway Things Manual"
.SH NAME
sway\-things \- Read and change the settings of Sway Things
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsway\-things\fR [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read and change the settings of Sway Things
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Controls when to use color
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
sway\-things\-get(1)
Show the value in effect and where it comes from; without a key, every stored setting
.TP
sway\-things\-set(1)
Change a setting: live, in the settings files and in the generated sway config
.TP
sway\-things\-reset(1)
Remove the stored value of a setting and apply its default
.TP
sway\-things\-show\-generated(1)
Print the generated sway config files as they would be written, without writing them
.TP
sway\-things\-doctor(1)
Check why settings might not take effect: the compositor, your sway config and its include line, the settings files, the generated files and the lines of your config that win
.TP
sway\-things\-open(1)
Start the app, or bring its window up if it runs, at a page or a setting
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
Done.
.TP
\fB1\fR
Failure: sway rejected a command or a generated file, a file can\*(Aqt be read or written, there is no sway to ask, or the app can\*(Aqt be found or started. For doctor: \-\-fix couldn\*(Aqt write the generated files.
.TP
\fB2\fR
Wrong arguments: an unknown key or page, a value the setting doesn\*(Aqt take, or \-\-device for a setting that isn\*(Aqt per device.
.TP
\fB3\fR
Read\-only: your sway config doesn\*(Aqt include the generated files yet, so nothing was changed. sway\-things doctor shows the line to add.
.TP
\fB4\fR
Refused: a risky setting without a terminal or \-\-yes, a change that wasn\*(Aqt kept, a setting the compositor doesn\*(Aqt support, or a generated file that was changed outside and not overwritten.
.TP
\fB5\fR
doctor found at least one problem, also after \-\-fix.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBSWAYSOCK\fR
The IPC socket of the running sway session, which changes are sent to.
.TP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR
Where the settings files, the generated files and your sway config are; ~/.config if unset.
.TP
\fBXDG_STATE_HOME\fR
Where the list of generated files and the history of the settings files are; ~/.local/state if unset.
.TP
\fBSWAY_THINGS_GUI\fR
The binary of the app for open, ahead of the one next to sway\-things and the one in PATH.
.TP
\fBSWAY_THINGS_LOCALEDIR\fR
The directory of the translations, ahead of the one set at build time.
.TP
\fBLANGUAGE, LC_ALL, LC_MESSAGES, LANG\fR
The language of the messages, as gettext reads them.
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR, CLICOLOR, CLICOLOR_FORCE\fR
Whether \-\-color auto colors the output.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/sway\-things/settings.toml\fR
The settings shared by all machines, e.g. in your dotfiles.
.TP
\fI~/.config/sway\-things/settings.d/<hostname>.toml\fR
The settings of this machine, ahead of the shared ones.
.TP
\fI~/.config/sway/sway\-things/*.conf\fR
The generated sway config files, which your sway config includes. Sway Things never writes your own config.
.TP
\fI~/.local/state/sway\-things/\fR
The list of generated files and the history of the settings files.
.SH VERSION
v0.0.0
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBsway\-things\-get\fR(1), \fBsway\-things\-set\fR(1), \fBsway\-things\-reset\fR(1), \fBsway\-things\-show\-generated\fR(1), \fBsway\-things\-doctor\fR(1), \fBsway\-things\-open\fR(1), \fBsway\-things\-gui\fR(1), \fBsway\fR(1), \fBsway\fR(5)
